A CI/CD question that surprises many candidates:

“The pipeline succeeded… but the deployment failed in production. What could be wrong?”

At first, this sounds confusing.

If the pipeline is green, everything should work… right?

Not always.

A successful pipeline only means the build and deployment steps completed.

It does not guarantee the application is healthy.

Here’s how experienced engineers investigate 

---

When deployment succeeds but the app fails:

✔ Environment variables missing or incorrect
✔ Secrets not available in runtime environment
✔ Database migrations not executed
✔ Config maps not updated
✔ Image tag mismatch between build & deploy
✔ Health checks failing after startup
✔ Incompatible dependency versions

Sometimes the deployment is perfect…

…but the app crashes due to missing config.
…or connects to the wrong database.
…or fails health checks and gets restarted.

---

Quick checks:

• verify runtime environment variables
• confirm secrets & config maps
• check pod logs after startup
• validate image version deployed
• ensure migrations ran successfully

---

Interview insight

If you say “pipeline passed so deployment is fine,”
it shows limited understanding.

If you investigate runtime configuration and environment differences,
it shows real-world DevOps thinking.

That’s what interviewers want.

---

A green pipeline doesn’t guarantee a healthy application.
